title: April 2024

@local_election_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Czarzasty, Biedroń and the local organisers now receive a political verdict rather than a model explanation, with retained aftermaths for rebuilding, dependence or purge.
title: The local-election verdict
subtitle: Organisation, polling and local alliances now change the result
face-image: img/poland/events/local-election-2024.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 29
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 4
on-arrival: {!
const localRoll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 5) - 2;
// March's hundred-day answer is three weeks old and decides whether these
// councillors ran under their own name or under the government's number.
const konkretyLocal =
    (Q.konkrety_audit_response == "Separate campaign"
        ? 2 + Math.min(2, Number(Q.konkrety_left_credit) || 0)
        : 0) +
    (Q.konkrety_audit_response == "Counter-audit" ? 1 : 0) +
    (Q.konkrety_audit_response == "Confrontation" ? 1 : 0) +
    (Q.konkrety_audit_response == "Defended the count"
        ? ((Number(Q.konkrety_delivered) || 0) < 10 ? -3 : -2)
        : 0);
const localScore =
    (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) * 0.20 +
    (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) * 0.65 +
    (Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 0) * 0.08 +
    (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 0) * 0.025 +
    konkretyLocal +
    localRoll;
Q.local_election_seats = Math.max(
    4,
    Math.min(32, Math.round(localScore))
);
Q.local_election_outcome =
    Q.local_election_seats >= 18
        ? "breakthrough"
        : (Q.local_election_seats >= 11 ? "mixed result" : "warning");
const advisorRoster = [
    ["miller", "Leszek Miller"],
    ["czarzasty", "Włodzimierz Czarzasty"],
    ["biedron", "Robert Biedroń"],
    ["zandberg", "Adrian Zandberg"],
    ["dziemianowicz_bak", "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk"],
    ["zukowska", "Anna-Maria Żukowska"],
    ["kotula", "Katarzyna Kotula"],
    ["biejat", "Magdalena Biejat"],
    ["wieczorek", "Dariusz Wieczorek"],
    ["gawkowski", "Krzysztof Gawkowski"],
    ["nowicka", "Wanda Nowicka"],
    ["zawisza", "Marcelina Zawisza"],
    ["matysiak", "Paulina Matysiak"],
    ["konieczny", "Wojciech Konieczny"],
    ["morawska_stanecka", "Gabriela Morawska-Stanecka"],
    ["kwiatkowski", "Robert Kwiatkowski"],
    ["pelczynska_nalecz", "Katarzyna Pełczyńska-Nałęcz"],
    ["hennig_kloska", "Paulina Hennig-Kloska"],
    ["zielinska", "Urszula Zielińska"],
    ["morawiecki", "Mateusz Morawiecki"],
    ["holownia", "Szymon Hołownia"],
    ["tracz", "Małgorzata Tracz"],
    ["spurek", "Sylwia Spurek"],
    ["semieniuk", "Olga Semeniuk-Patkowska"],
    ["cieszynski", "Janusz Cieszyński"]
];
const activeAdvisorNames = advisorRoster
    .filter(function(advisor) {
        return Number(Q[advisor[0] + "_advisor"]) === 1;
    })
    .map(function(advisor) {
        return advisor[1];
    });
const liveLeadership = String(Q.left_leader || "").trim();
const defaultLeadership = "Włodzimierz Czarzasty and Robert Biedroń";
if (!activeAdvisorNames.length) {
    Q.local_election_leaders = "the party leadership";
} else if (liveLeadership && liveLeadership !== defaultLeadership) {
    Q.local_election_leaders = liveLeadership;
} else if (activeAdvisorNames.length === 1) {
    Q.local_election_leaders = activeAdvisorNames[0];
} else if (activeAdvisorNames.length === 2) {
    Q.local_election_leaders =
        activeAdvisorNames[0] + " and " + activeAdvisorNames[1];
} else {
    Q.local_election_leaders =
        activeAdvisorNames.slice(0, -1).join(", ") +
        ", and " +
        activeAdvisorNames[activeAdvisorNames.length - 1];
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left wins " + Q.local_election_seats +
    " regional seats in a " + Q.local_election_outcome;
!}

= April 2024 — [+ local_election_seats +] regional seats

Party leaders **[+ local_election_leaders +]** receive the provincial maps
at a headquarters crowded with candidates who have spent months asking for
staff, money and permission to make local bargains. The count is a **[+
local_election_outcome +]**.

[? if local_election_outcome = "breakthrough": New councillors enter regional
assemblies with enough colleagues to demand offices and policy, but not enough
to live without municipal allies.?][? if local_election_outcome = "mixed result":
Strong counties sit beside blank areas where the national logo never became an
organisation.?][? if local_election_outcome = "warning": Regional organisers
have lost seats, deposits and the argument that television polling can replace
people known in a district.?]

[? if konkrety_audit_response = "Separate campaign": The regions ran these
three weeks on our own promises rather than on the government's hundred, which
is why the ballots carry our name where they carry anything at all.?]
[? if konkrety_audit_response = "Defended the count": The regions ran these
three weeks defending a government scoreboard reading [+ konkrety_delivered +]
out of a hundred. Candidates who were asked about it on doorsteps report that
the conversation rarely recovered.?]
[? if konkrety_audit_response = "Counter-audit": Our hundred-day audit is still
being quoted, and in the county towns it did the one thing a national document
can do for a local campaign: it gave canvassers an answer.?]
[? if konkrety_audit_response = "Confrontation": The chamber row with the Prime
Minister ran for a fortnight and reached voters who have never watched a
parliamentary sitting. It also cost the transfers that several of our
candidates were counting on.?]
[? if konkrety_audit_response = "Written re-plan": The re-planned konkrety
carry dates now, which is worth a great deal in 2026 and nothing whatever on a
ballot paper in April.?]

The choice is what headquarters does to the people behind the map: bind itself
to a four-year rebuild, shelter under KO mayors, or punish the regions and take
their nominations back to Warsaw.

Wrocław makes the choice concrete. **Jacek Sutryk** enters the mayoral runoff
against Third Way-backed **Izabela Bodnar** carrying the Collegium Humanum
story and the weight of a municipal machine. Bodnar's campaign is itself hit
by allegations concerning her family's business. Neither set of allegations
is a verdict of guilt; both make any endorsement a test of what Lewica accepts
from a local ally.

- @local_rebuild
- @local_ko
- @local_blame

@local_rebuild
title: Put the parliamentary delegation on a four-year local rebuilding contract
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Send MPs and organisers back to weak counties; governing work loses some attention while the party grows roots.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The centre cannot finance a national organiser corps.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.local_network += 8;
Q.barons_dissent -= 2;
if (Q.left_in_government) Q.government_delivery -= 1;
Q.party_unity += 2;
(typeof window !== "undefined" ? window : globalThis).polandElectionModel
    .recordRegionalEffect(Q, {
        key: "wroclaw-2024-conditional-sutryk",
        families: {left: 0.12}, countyIds: ["0264"]
    });
Q.news_headline = "The Left conditionally backs Sutryk and rebuilds in Wrocław";
!}

Every deputy receives counties, organisers and a date by which a local slate
must exist without a national campaign visit. Regional leaders keep their
knowledge and gain a contract headquarters can be judged against.

[? if left_in_government: Ministers lose some parliamentary attention to party
work.?] In Wrocław support for Sutryk is conditional on transparent municipal
appointments and cooperation with Left councillors. The immediate media cycle
passes without a scapegoat. Four years from
now, there will either be candidates where the map is blank or no excuse left
for the centre.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the rebuilding contract on the events desk

@local_ko
title: Trade endorsements and accept dependence on KO mayors
subtitle: Save offices through municipal cooperation; local barons survive by making Lewica useful to a stronger partner.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ko_relation += 7;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.barons_dissent += 5;
Q.party_unity -= 2;
(typeof window !== "undefined" ? window : globalThis).polandElectionModel
    .recordRegionalEffect(Q, {
        key: "wroclaw-2024-ko-bargain",
        families: {ko: 0.10, left: 0.04}, countyIds: ["0264"]
    });
Q.news_headline = "Sutryk drifts toward KO while Lewica keeps a smaller Wrocław foothold";
!}

Our councillors trade second-round endorsements and committee votes for places
inside administrations led by KO mayors. Services keep experienced Lewica
officials and some losing candidates retain public work.

Each agreement is locally rational. Together they teach organisers that the
shortest route to office runs through another party, while the regional barons
gain private leverage over a centre which cannot replace those relationships.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the municipal bargains on the events desk

@local_blame
title: Replace regional leaders and centralise candidate selection
subtitle: Give the count a visible culprit and Warsaw a stronger hand; discard relationships the next local campaign still needs.
on-arrival: {!
Q.barons_strength -= 4;
Q.progressives_strength += 3;
Q.local_network -= 4;
Q.party_unity -= 4;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
(typeof window !== "undefined" ? window : globalThis).polandElectionModel
    .recordRegionalEffect(Q, {
        key: "wroclaw-2024-withdrawal",
        families: {left: -0.08}, countyIds: ["0264"]
    });
Q.news_headline = "Lewica withdraws from Sutryk and centralises its Wrocław organisation";
!}

Regional chairs are removed before they finish explaining the precinct maps.
Younger figures receive nominations from Warsaw and the co-chairs can tell the
cameras that the warning has consequences.

The dismissed leaders take councillors, donor lists and grudges with them.
Central control wins the week in which failure is assigned and loses people
who knew which county hall would open its door next time.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the regional purge on the events desk

@abortion_first_reading
# prose-audit: Grade A — Kotula, Lempart, Kosiniak-Kamysz, patients and clinicians now expose what the four bills divide, and each Lewica strategy retains a distinct coalition and movement consequence.
title: Four abortion bills survive first reading
subtitle: Agreement on debate conceals four different endpoints
face-image: img/poland/events/womens-strike-2020.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 28
order: 11
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 4 and government_party != "pis" and caretaker_government = 0 and abortion_reform_settled = 0
on-arrival: feminist_trust += 2; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 12; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += 6; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_backlash += 6; news_headline = "The coalition advances four incompatible abortion bills"

= April 2024 — Four bills enter one committee

The Sejm has refused to kill any of the four abortion bills at first reading.
That shared vote hides incompatible destinations: decriminalisation, legal
abortion through twelve weeks, a narrower restoration and a referendum route.

Lewica MP and equality campaigner Katarzyna Kotula wants the committee to know
its destination before compromise begins. Marta Lempart, co-founder of the
All-Poland Women's Strike, wants women and clinicians to see law change before
another parliamentary season disappears. PSL leader Władysław
Kosiniak-Kamysz will not promise his deputies to either project.

We can make twelve weeks the coalition test, sequence the reforms, organise a
free vote district by district, or declare decriminalisation enough and move
the party back toward material conflict. A committee has created time, not a
majority.

- @abortion_max
- @abortion_sequence
- @abortion_free
- @abortion_material_truce

@abortion_max
title: Make restoration through twelve weeks the coalition test
subtitle: Give Kotula and the movement an unambiguous endpoint; [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl": force PSL to decide whether it remains in the coalition.?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": make opposition PSL vote without pretending it can leave the cabinet.?]
on-arrival: abortion_strategy = "Twelve-week coalition test"; feminist_trust += 6; progressive_credibility += 5; psl_relation -= 10; government_coalition_dissent += 7 if left_in_government = 1; barons_dissent += 3; news_headline = "The Left names the endpoint before the coalition has the votes"

Kotula puts the twelve-week bill first in every coalition meeting and Lempart
can tell the street exactly what Lewica is trying to pass. Patients and doctors
gain a clear legal destination, not another promise to improve the compromise.

Kosiniak-Kamysz tells PSL deputies that the issue is outside party discipline.
We have made the test legible before assembling the votes. [? if
ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl": The cabinet now
carries the resulting fracture into every other negotiation.?][? if
ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": PSL can withhold its
votes, but it cannot fracture a cabinet it never joined.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Put the twelve-week test on the events desk

@abortion_sequence
title: Pass decriminalisation first and build clinical access behind it
subtitle: Remove criminal exposure before testing the full access bill; movement allies may hear another postponement of the endpoint.
on-arrival: abortion_strategy = "Decriminalisation sequence"; feminist_trust += 4; government_delivery += 2 if left_in_government = 1; psl_relation -= 5; ko_relation += 3; razem_dissent += 2; news_headline = "The Left chooses a sequenced reproductive-rights campaign"

The first whip count moves to penalties faced by patients, relatives and
clinicians. KO can join a measure framed around ending prosecution while the
committee continues work on legal access.

The sequence can change somebody's immediate risk and build a larger majority.
It also asks the Women's Strike to believe that *first* will not again become
*instead*; Razem records that reservation beside its support.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the legislative sequence on the events desk

@abortion_free
title: Accept a free vote and organise constituency pressure
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Let every deputy choose, then make that choice visible to patients and organisers in the district.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party lacks a national pressure campaign.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; abortion_strategy = "Free vote with constituency pressure"; feminist_trust += 3; psl_relation += 2; local_network += 3; government_coalition_dissent -= 2; progressives_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Every undecided deputy receives a district campaign"

PSL keeps its free vote. [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party =
"psl": The coalition avoids a formal rupture.?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet =
0 and government_party != "psl": No coalition rupture was PSL's to threaten;
the bargain concerns parliamentary votes only.?] In exchange, our organisers
publish local meetings, clinic testimony and the names of every undecided
deputy long before the division bell.

Kosiniak-Kamysz gains room inside his party; his MPs lose anonymity at home.
The movement receives a campaign rather than a guarantee, and some
progressives ask why government power has become another petition drive.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the constituency campaign to the events desk

@abortion_material_truce
title: Accept decriminalisation as a ceiling and move the campaign to wages and housing
subtitle: Opens the developmental-conservative path; PSL and Poland 2050 relations improve, but feminist trust falls.
on-arrival: abortion_strategy = "Material compromise"; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience -= 12; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience -= 5; public_mood_pending_secular_state_salience -= 4; cultural_issue_salience -= 7; economic_issue_salience += 7; left_right_score += 6; left_cultural_position += 5; social_patriot_support += 8; matysiak_development_pressure += 8; psl_relation += 7; p2050_relation += 5; feminist_trust -= 7; progressives_dissent += 9; spring_dissent += 6; razem_dissent += 7; labor_credibility += 3; news_headline = "Lewica treats decriminalisation as a truce and returns to material conflict"

We tell the committee that ending criminal penalties is the reform this
coalition can carry and move our principal demands back to wages, housing and
public investment. [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party =
"psl": PSL hears a partner making room for it.?][? if
ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": PSL hears an
opponent making room for a future vote or coalition.?] Polska 2050 hears the
same offer;
the developmental current sees a new organising line.

Lempart and Kotula hear the party declare a ceiling before the vote. The truce
calms the coalition by transferring the conflict into Lewica, where feminist,
Wiosna and Razem organisers now have to decide whether material politics was
offered as an addition or an exit.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the material truce on the events desk
